WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.920
So at the moment if we want to 
measure what the brain is doing,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.940
if we want to measure brain function,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.520
there are a few ways of doing it but one way is Magnetoencephalography, or MEG.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.880
The idea of MEG is that we measure 
magnetic fields that exist outside the head

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.940
that are generated by current flow in the brain

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.540
and in that way we can work out 
what the brain was doing at any one time.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.400
The problem with current MEG scanners

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.560
is that they're very large, they're very bulky

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.560
and they're one-size-fits-all.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.240
The gap in the market, 
if that's the right expression,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.730
is for a scanner which you can wear on your head.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.220
So you put it on like a helmet, 
you can wear it on your head

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.780
whilst we're acquiring brain imaging data.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.340
So to build a wearable imaging system
you really need two things.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:03.100
You need very, very sensitive magnetic field sensors

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.940
that are small, lightweight 
and that can go on the head

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.611
and that's what we had with the quantum sensors

00:01:07.611 --> 00:01:11.301
and then you need a way 
to house them on the head.

00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:15.260
And so to do that we built a 3D-printed head cast

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.520
and that would house the quantum sensors 
close to the scalp.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.160
And that was designed based on 
a single subject's head shape.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.680
I volunteered to be that subject and yeah, that's...

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.980
...so this helmet accommodates 13 sensors

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:37.060
which are over the motor region,

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.340
the right motor region of my brain.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.940
I'm putting it all together.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.360
It just fits....

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.860
Yeah, so it fits perfectly on my head.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.180
The quantum sensors give us 
the magnetic fields

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.440
that are produced by our brain at any one time.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.460
And by knowing also the location of these
sensors with respect to the brain,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.680
we can localize which area
of the brain was responsible for the movement

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:22.480
and also when that part of the
brain was engaged in that certain task.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.980
Ideally we would be looking at 
something more generic

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.740
like, something like a bike helmet

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.560
which could be adaptable 
to any anyone's head size

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.940
and could just hold the sensors

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:43.060
without having to build something 
specifically for just one person.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.480
There are a number of challenges but
probably the biggest one we had was

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.000
reducing the Earth's magnetic field.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.400
So if you want somebody to be able
to move with a scanner on their head,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.500
and that scanner's measuring magnetic fields,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.500
you need to somehow remove 
the Earth's magnetic field.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.300
So when they told me on day one that my
job was going to be

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.960
to remove the Earth's magnetic field

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.280
that sounded more like a joke they tell 
to new starters than anything else.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.320
The way we went about this was to 
build these new electromagnetic coils

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.720
that produce fields that are equal and opposite

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.000
to the Earth's magnetic field.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.980
So the mathematics required to design these coils to reduce the magnetic field

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.360
is actually quite complex, 
it's quite a large challenge,

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.460
but then once you've got past all of that
 the actual making of the coils is

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:33.000
bits of wood, bits of masking tape, 
bits of glue and bits of wire,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.260
so it's a massive contrast really 
in what you're doing.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.480
They're housed on two planes 
either side of the subject,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.580
so you've got one going down here,
one going down here.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.760
And that keeps the scanner quite open, you can walk in and out of it.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.120
Crucially it meant that the sensors wouldn't fail

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.480
if the subject moved
even by a tiny amount,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.820
and that meant that any information 
we were getting from the sensors

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.360
we knew was coming from the brain and that we 
would be able to do these cool experiments.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.320
With this new technology,

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.940
scanning babies, two-year-olds, 
three-year-olds, four-year-olds

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.740
is going to become possible.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:12.200
So that brings into play 
a number of different disorders

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.820
like epilepsy but also things like autism.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.840
I think we will certainly be able
to really start seeing

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.580
the neural substrates that underlie 
these disorders in children.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.720
Should I get this rid of this?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.820
It's up to you!

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.200
[laughter]

